 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Camera Convention:** Incorrect conversion to Blender convention (flipping Y and Z) will result in inverted or rotated views, breaking multi-view consistency [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Timestep Range:** Using the full range `[0, 1]` may lead to unstable gradients. The default `[0.02, 0.98]` avoids extreme noise levels [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Guidance Scale:** A high guidance scale (e.g., 100) can lead to over-saturation or artifacts if not balanced with other losses [S2, unofficial].
+*   **CFG Chunking:** The model output must be chunkable along the batch dimension into exactly two equal parts for conditional and unconditional predictions [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Timestep Bounds:** Sampling outside the `[min_step, max_step]` range may produce unstable gradients or invalid noise predictions [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Camera Indexing:** The column reordering `[0, 2, 1, 3]` assumes a specific 4x4 pose layout; incorrect input dimensions will cause indexing errors [S1, unofficial].
